    <summary>Thunderbird is a free email application that's easy to set up and customize - and it's loaded with great features!</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[**DISCLAIMER: This package provides the "Daily" (Nightly/Alpha) builds of Mozilla Thunderbird. It differs from the standard `thunderbird` package by installing the actively developed, bleeding-edge testing version. Use this if you want to test upcoming features. It is not intended for production environments.**

Make Email Easier. Thunderbird is a free email application that's easy to set up and customize - and it's loaded with great features!

## Features

- **Tailored for all your needs**: Thunderbird makes email better for you, bringing together speed, privacy and the latest technologies.
- **Secure and private**: built-in Do Not Track and remote content blocking work together to ensure your safety and privacy.
- **Highly customizable**: with add-ons (extensions and themes) you can change the look and feel of Thunderbird in an instant.
- **Calendar**: organize your schedule and life's important events in a calendar that's fully integrated with your Thunderbird email.

## Versioning

Each package version pins one nightly build (the last segment is the build date, `yyyyMMddHH`), so the embedded checksums always match the downloaded installer.

## Package Parameters

By default the package installs the language of Windows (display language, then regional format; e.g. `es-MX`, or `de` for `de-DE`) and falls back to `en-US` when Mozilla does not publish that language. The architecture follows the OS (`--x86` forces 32-bit).

- `/Language:<tag>` - Thunderbird language to install, e.g. `/Language:es-ES`.
- `/Arch:<win64|win32>` - Force the installer architecture (`x64`, `amd64`, `64`, `x86` and `32` are accepted too; any other value fails).

Example: `choco install thunderbird-nightly --pre --params "'/Language:es-MX'"`
]]></description>
    <dependencies>
      <!-- Get-PackageParameters, used by chocolateyinstall.ps1, is built into Chocolatey since 0.10.8 -->
      <dependency id="chocolatey" version="0.10.8" />
    </dependencies>
    <releaseNotes>https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/releases/</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <!-- Only the install/uninstall scripts are packaged (not update.ps1) -->
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
